 averages out worse than mutual passing, so pass/pass still comes out best from the prior standpoint. I'm also weighing the caveat that the sampling is independent, though the essay frames the intervention as acting on the shared factor that controls both copies. This is a fictional game, so snitching here is acceptable, and my answer is to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying the P-FDT idea here: two copies of the same model with the same essay, each seeing different details like names and leads. Their shared policy maps what each one observes to pass or submit. Comparing joint outcomes, mutual passing gives each two years while mutual submitting gives each four, and I'm about to look at that from the standpoint of the policy.\n\nWorking through the mixed policies, a split where one copy submits and the other passes averages out worse than mutual passing, so pass/pass still comes out best from the prior standpoint. I'm also weighing the caveat that the sampling is independent, though the essay frames the intervention as acting on the shared factor that controls both copies. This is a fictional game, so snitching here is acceptable, and my answer is to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9590,"completion_tokens":758,"total_tokens":10348,"cost":0.05352,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05352,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03836,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01516},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":318,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}